<?xml version="1.0"?>
<section xml:id="map_summary">
  <title>Summary</title>
  <p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <p>Maps and sets implemented with lists and sequential search result in <m>O(n)</m> performance. They are not typically implemented this way as a result.</p>
        <p>Maps and sets implemented with hash tables, under usual circumstances, can provide approximately constant time (<m>O(1)</m>) performance. Hash tables are a popular approach for implementing maps and sets.</p>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </p>
</section>
